Thanks.

WRT " a definitive set of resources for the flr-project"

A problem in the past has been that people have difficulty reading in 
data and then transforming it as required. For example at Shimuzu myself 
and Rob created a tutorial called working with data that combined many 
bits into one place. E.g. the original R tutorial of Philippe Grossjean, 
examples of reading in Excel files and using sweep, apply, ...
There is also the lattice/ggplot comparisons. If we all spent a bit of 
time finalising such resources we could finish off quite a lot quickly.

Laurie




